  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal would result in a significant and unacceptable reduction in daylight to habitable rooms of flats at 52 and 54 Burlington Road. The proposal would be contrary to Policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012 and Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The proposed development, due to lack of private balconies for Units 6 and 7, and an insufficient quantum of communal amenity space, fails to provide a suitable level of outdoor amenity for future occupants, contrary to LP Policy D6, Policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012 and Policy Guidance 13 and 14 in the Residential Design Supplementary Planning Document 2013.",
    "In the absence of a legal agreement to ensure that future occupants of the proposed development would be precluded from obtaining on-street car parking permits, the proposed development would lead to inconsiderate parking and increase on-street car parking pressure and congestion in surrounding streets.  As such, the proposal is considered to conflict with Policy T6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM10 of the adopted Core Strategy 2012.\r"
  ],
